        {
          "duration": {
            "from": 886.53925,
            "to": 896.53925
          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>On immunohistochemistry of a lymph node excision biopsy, the neoplastic cells st</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>On immunohistochemistry of a lymph node excision biopsy, the neoplastic cells stain positive for CD20 and negative for both CD15 and CD30. Which subtype of Hodgkin lymphoma does this immunophenotype indicate?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Nodular sclerosis classical Hodgkin lymphoma</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Nodular sclerosis is a classical HL subtype whose Reed-Sternberg cells are CD15+, CD30+, and CD45−, not CD20+. It is characterised by collagen bands and lacunar cells.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mixed cellularity classical Hodgkin lymphoma</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Mixed cellularity is also a classical subtype with the standard CD15+/CD30+/CD45− profile. It features classic binucleate RS cells in an eosinophil-rich background.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. NLPHL is defined by popcorn (LP) cells that are CD20+, CD15−, and CD30− — the immunophenotypic opposite of classical HL. It follows an indolent clinical course.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Lymphocyte-depleted classical Hodgkin lymphoma</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Lymphocyte-depleted HL belongs to the classical group and shares the CD15+/CD30+/CD45− profile. It is characterised by mummified RS cells and carries the most aggressive course among classical subtypes.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "All four classical HL subtypes show CD15+/CD30+/CD45− Reed-Sternberg cells. When neoplastic cells are instead CD20+/CD15−/CD30−, the diagnosis is nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma, defined by its popcorn (LP) cells."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. A CD20+/CD15−/CD30− profile identifies NLPHL, whose popcorn cells have the opposite immunophenotype to classical Hodgkin lymphoma. This distinction matters because NLPHL follows an indolent course with different management."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
